			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4056884">
									

<blockquote>
<p>See, and this was meant to be JUST fluff.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Sure, and that's why the fluff to crunch ratio is not to my preference.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This is an in character message the players read, to introduce them to the setting, and see what is there. It's not meant to be entirely relegion focused, it's just that there were a LOT of gods to go over.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>For this kind of thing I would prefer something like the player's guides to Pathfinder Adventurer Paths. There's an opportunity here to give setting specific character options that players can use to make their characters really part of this setting and this campaign specifically, rather than making Genero Boringfoot of the Underplace Boringfoots, Halfling, Rogue/1 that they could have in any game.</p>
<p>The audience that's not your gaming group (I.e. us) isn't going to be playing in your game, and, for me, there's not much here that I have any use for.</p>

							</div>

								
